ion/worked-solution" "value" "If we let $u=3x,$ then\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=3\\,⟹\\,\\frac{1}{3}\\text{d}u=\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nComputing our limits of integration, we get the following:\n\n| $x$ | $0$ | $\\operatorname{ln}⁡4$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $u$ | $0$ | $3\\operatorname{ln}⁡4$ |\n\nThen, we can write the integral in terms of $u$ and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡4}5{e}^{3x}\\,\\text{d}x & =5{\\int }_{0}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡4}{e}^{3x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =5{\\int }_{0}^{3\\operatorname{ln}⁡4}{e}^{u}\\cdot \\frac{1}{3}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{3}{\\int }_{0}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡({4}^{3})}{e}^{u}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{3}\\cdot {e}^{u}\\,{|}_{0}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡({4}^{3})} \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{3}({e}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡({4}^{3})}-{e}^{0}) \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{3}({4}^{3}-1) \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{3}(64-1) \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{3}(63) \\\\  & =105\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14028924/state.json" "file_sha256" "c22cf7f0dbc285a1a217a2c0ab768006228ca003815a9e100d048618533b3744"} {"question" "q-349596" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14028924/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "b2eb951cb3d36b14d96017da3418997a02a66b8f7e27d6df22722526b30e7a32"} {"question" "q-349596" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14028924/state.json" "file_sha256" "c22cf7f0dbc285a1a217a2c0ab768006228ca003815a9e100d048618533b3744"} {"question" "q-349596" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "105"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14028924/state.json" "file_sha256" "c22cf7f0dbc285a1a217a2c0ab768006228ca003815a9e100d048618533b3744"} {"question" "q-349625" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Evaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\int }_{1}^{2}{3}^{7-2x}\\,\\text{d}x=$  \n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14028924/state.json" "file_sha256" "c22cf7f0dbc285a1a217a2c0ab768006228ca003815a9e100d048618533b3744"} {"question" "q-349625" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "If we let $u=7-2x,$ then\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=-2\\,⟹\\,-\\frac{1}{2}\\,\\text{d}u=\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nComputing our limits of integration, we get the following:\n\n| $x$ | $1$ | $2$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $u$ | $5$ | $3$ |\n\nThen, we can write the integral in terms of $u$ and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{1}^{2}{3}^{7-2x}\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{5}^{3}{3}^{u}(-\\frac{1}{2})\\text{d}u \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{5}^{3}{3}^{u}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{2}(\\frac{{3}^{u}}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}){|}_{5}^{3} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{2\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}({3}^{3}-{3}^{5}) \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{2\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}(27-243) \\\\  & =\\frac{108}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14028924/state.json" "file_sha256" "c22cf7f0dbc285a1a217a2c0ab768006228ca003815a9e100d048618533b3744"} {"question" "q-349625" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14028924/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "b2eb951cb3d36b14d96017da3418997a02a66b8f7e27d6df22722526b30e7a32"} {"question" "q-349625" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14028924/state.json" "file_sha256" "c22cf7f0dbc285a1a217a2c0ab768006228ca003815a9e100d048618533b3744"} {"question" "q-349625" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{108}{\\ln(3)}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14028924/state.json" "file_sha256" "c22cf7f0dbc285a1a217a2c0ab768006228ca003815a9e100d048618533b3744"} {"question" "q-362689" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Evaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\int }_{-1}^{0}12{e}^{-4x}\\,\\text{d}x=$  \n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14028924/state.json" "file_sha256" "c22cf7f0dbc285a1a217a2c0ab768006228ca003815a9e100d048618533b3744"} {"question" "q-362689" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "If we let $u=-4x,$ then\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=-4\\,⟹\\,-\\frac{1}{4}\\text{d}u=\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nComputing our limits of integration, we get the following:\n\n| $x$ | $-1$ | $0$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $u$ | $4$ | $0$ |\n\nThen, we can write the integral in terms of $u$ and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-1}^{0}12{e}^{-4x}\\,\\text{d}x & =12{\\int }_{-1}^{0}{e}^{-4x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =12{\\int }_{4}^{0}{e}^{u}\\cdot (-\\frac{1}{4})\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =-3{\\int }_{4}^{0}{e}^{u}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =-3\\cdot {e}^{u}\\,{|}_{4}^{0} \\\\  & =-3({e}^{0}-{e}^{4}) \\\\  & =-3(1-{e}^{4}) \\\\  & =3{e}^{4}-3\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14028924/state.json" "file_sha256" "c22cf7f0dbc285a1a217a2c0ab768006228ca003815a9e100d048618533b3744"} {"question" "q-362689" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficu